caption: CASUALTY MODEL
campaign-component: casualty-model

SUPERSEDED BASELINE: Without rapid intervention, the catastrophe was projected to cause approximately 2.1 million deaths, 6–10 million injuries, and 15–25 million displaced people. Most deaths would have come from prolonged Gate incursions, monsters, fire, and delayed infrastructure failure rather than the original spell.

PROVISIONAL: If the party had closed essentially all Gates within the first one to three hours, approximately 175,000–450,000 deaths would have been plausible.

CURRENT PROVISIONAL MODEL: Because twelve maintained Gates resist closure and create sustained incursions, 300,000 deaths is now optimistic.

CURRENT PROVISIONAL RANGE:

- If most maintained Gates are neutralized within two or three hours: approximately 400,000–700,000 deaths.

- If several major Gates persist into the night: more than 1 million deaths.

- Injuries remain in the millions.

- Displacement remains approximately 12–20 million people.

- Final casualty figures must be recalculated after the exact invasion forces, Gate duration, and party response timeline are fixed.

LOCKED: The party still saves approximately one to two million people compared with an unopposed catastrophe.
